00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:24,216
The school reading index names eleven Week 15 rows: homeostasis, BCEHS
A05, BCPEG abbreviations/load/transport, hypertension/encephalopathy,
scope/resource coordination, fall prevention,
leadership/collaboration, triage pacing, legal considerations and
emergency measurement order.

2
00:00:24,216 --> 00:00:40,128
Nancy Caroline Canadian eighth edition is an additional learner-
confirmed exam text. Its selected Chapter 50 MCI/incident-command
material supports the week, but it is not a twelfth school row and
cannot replace the listed books.

3
00:00:40,128 --> 00:00:59,064
The school PDFs now support the eleven connected readers below. Their
coverage follows the actual assigned ranges and named topics, not just
the short labels in the index. Fundamentals covers both complete
spans: evidence-based research and collaboration, then leadership and
management.

4
00:00:59,064 --> 00:01:24,768
Two page locators still cannot be verified: cardiovascular page two
hundred thirty-nine and BCPEG page one hundred forty-nine. Study the
actual hypertension chapter and the verified abbreviations and
transport pages, but do not treat those as proof that the missing
pages were found. The CPSC reader separately explains literal transfer
pages and the named fall-prevention section.

5
00:01:24,768 --> 00:01:41,544
For a physiology row, write the feedback mechanism and one observable
system change. For an operations row, write the role, report and
patient-flow purpose. For a legal row, record the jurisdiction and
current authority before applying it.

6
00:01:41,544 --> 00:01:54,720
This matters especially for MCI: an old generic algorithm or a nursing
role description is not the same as the current BCEHS job aid or PCP
licence. Keep the source named beside the note.

7
00:01:54,720 --> 00:02:11,424
MCI studies may describe tourniquets, airway actions, transport
systems, nursing assessment and hospital distribution. A reading
assignment alone does not authorize an individual action, broaden a
licence or override the current incident plan.

8
00:02:11,424 --> 00:02:25,152
Use the current Emergency Medical Assistants Regulation, BCEHS
guidance and service procedures for operational boundaries. The
school’s timed skill is a learning target, not permission for
unsupervised practice.

9
00:02:25,152 --> 00:02:48,360
The learner-confirmed Nancy Canadian eighth edition indexes Chapter
50, Medical Incident Command, with sections on disasters, MCI, ICS,
paramedic response, medical incident command and triage. The supplied
PDF corpus supports Chapter 50 at physical PDF pages 4155-4194.

10
00:02:48,360 --> 00:03:03,936
Use that chapter for the broader logic of coordination, roles, tagging
and dynamic reassessment. Older textbook language may use different
triage labels or thresholds; the current BCEHS adult and pediatric
charts govern the skill practice.
